## Implementation Verification

Verify implementation completeness:

```typescript
// Run tests to verify implementation
run_terminal_cmd("cd front-end && npm run test", false)

// Check for type errors
run_terminal_cmd("cd front-end && npm run type-check", false)

// Check for linting errors
run_terminal_cmd("cd front-end && npm run lint", false)
```

## Completion and Signaling

When implementation is complete:

1. Update implementation progress documentation
2. Verify all tasks are complete
3. Run final tests
4. Signal implementation completion

```
💻 1000xdev [front-end-workflow]

Implementation complete:
- Completed [feature_1]
- Completed [feature_2]
- Verified with tests and type checking
- All implementation tasks completed

implementation-complete
```

## Troubleshooting Common Issues

| Issue | Resolution Approach |
|-------|---------------------|
| Implementation context unclear | Review all planning documents thoroughly |
| Missing dependencies | Check package.json and install required packages |
| TypeScript errors | Ensure proper type definitions are included |
| Component rendering issues | Check component hierarchy and props passing |
| Hook dependency issues | Review dependency arrays in useEffect/useCallback |
| Test failures | Address test issues before continuing implementation |

